course: dictionary
lesson: 14124
title: Migratory: words in science
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Migratory describes animals that travel regularly from one place to another, usually with the seasons. «Swallows are migratory birds.» Swallows fly away when the weather turns cold and come back when it warms up, so migratory must mean moving from place to place with the seasons.
explain: Use the swap check. Put your meaning into the sentence: «Swallows are birds that move from place to place with the seasons.» It still makes sense, so your meaning is right.
explain: Migratory can also describe a path. «The geese followed a migratory route across the sea.» The route is the way the geese travel each year. In science, the same idea appears in words like migratory species, which means a kind of animal that migrates.
fact: Migratory means moving regularly from one place to another, usually with the seasons.
fact: Animals migrate to find food, warmth or a place to breed.
fact: «Migratory birds» are birds that travel with the seasons, such as swallows and geese.
fact: A «migratory route» is the path that animals take on their journeys, often every year.
fact: Migration is the journey itself; migratory is the describing word.
exercise: «Swallows are migratory birds, flying south when winter comes.» What does migratory mean? | Staying in one place all year | Able to swim well | Very fast and loud | *Moving regularly from place to place with the seasons
exercise: «The monarch butterflies follow a long migratory route each autumn.» What is a migratory route? | A bird's nest high in a tree | *The path that animals take on their regular journeys | A road made only for cars
exercise: Which of these animals is migratory? | A rock | A tree | A pebble on the beach | *An Arctic tern, which flies between the Arctic and Antarctic
test: «Whales have a migratory life, travelling thousands of miles between cold and warm seas.» What does migratory suggest here? | Sleeping all year round | *Travelling regularly from place to place | Being very small | Staying at the bottom of the sea
test: Which phrase means the same as a migratory route? | A plant that grows in water | *A path travelled regularly every year | A type of cake | A short walk to school
exam: Why are swallows called migratory birds? | They sing very loudly all year | They never leave their nests | They live only in cities | *They move from place to place with the seasons
